 OVERVIEW
 --------
 My Time gives every caller their own clock. A user in another time zone
 sets a personal offset from the BBS clock and from then on sees THEIR
 time, not the board's. The offset changes display only - the BBS's own
 timekeeping is never touched.

 COMMANDS (work at any prompt on the board)
 ------------------------------------------
   /time            show the BBS clock
   /mytime          show your clock
   /mytime +2       run 2 hours ahead of the BBS
   /mytime -1       run 1 hour behind the BBS
   /mytime +9:30    half-hour zones work too
   /mytime reset    match the BBS clock again
   /mytime ?        usage summary

 Offsets run from -23:59 to +23:59. New users are always on BBS time
 until they set an offset themselves.

 TEXT VARIABLES
 --------------
 My Time registers three named text variables you can embed in ANY
 message text on the board (menus included):

   MYTIME     the caller's time, h:mm with a/p     e.g. 10:00a, 9:05p
   MYT_BBS    the BBS time in the same format
   MYT_OFS    the caller's offset, signed          e.g. +2:00, -1:00

 With no offset set, MYTIME shows BBS time.

 SYSOP NOTES
 -----------
 - Installation: copy SNMYTIME.DLL, SNMYTIME.MDF, SNMYTIME.MSG and
   SNMYTIME.RLN into the BBS directory with the system shut down, then
   restart. My Time announces its version in the Audit Trail at startup.
 - No menu entry is needed (the MDF is UNCONDITIONAL / INTERNAL); the
   commands are global.
 - Per-user offsets are stored in the system's general user database.
   No extra data files are created or shipped. Deleting an account
   removes its stored offset.
 - Setting: "Log user time-offset changes to the Audit Trail" (default
   YES). The CNF option is the install default only; change it live with
   /mytime audit on  or  /mytime audit off  (SYSOP key required). The
   change applies immediately and is itself recorded in the Audit Trail.

